---
description: Standards for Python packaging implementation
globs: ["**/*.py"]
alwaysApply: true
---
# Python Packaging Standards

<rule>
name: python_packaging
description: Enforces Python packaging and distribution best practices
filters:
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\.py$|setup\.py$|pyproject\.toml$"

actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      ## Python Packaging Guidelines

      1. Project Structure
         - Use standard project layout
         - Separate source and tests
         - Include necessary package files
         - Use src layout when appropriate
         - Follow naming conventions

      2. Dependencies
         - Specify version ranges appropriately
         - Use dependency groups
         - Pin development dependencies
         - Document all dependencies
         - Use virtual environments

      3. Package Configuration
         - Use pyproject.toml for modern packaging
         - Include all necessary metadata
         - Specify Python version requirements
         - Define entry points properly
         - Include package data correctly

      4. Documentation
         - Maintain comprehensive README
         - Include installation instructions
         - Document all dependencies
         - Provide usage examples
         - Include contribution guidelines

      5. Distribution
         - Use proper version numbers
         - Create source distributions
         - Build wheel distributions
         - Sign package releases
         - Upload to PyPI securely

      6. Development Tools
         - Configure development tools properly
         - Use pre-commit hooks
         - Set up CI/CD pipelines
         - Include tox configuration
         - Configure coverage tools

examples:
  - input: |
      # Bad packaging
      setup(
          name="mypackage",
          version="1.0",
      )
      
      # Good packaging
      # pyproject.toml
      [build-system]
      requires = ["hatchling"]
      build-backend = "hatchling.build"
      
      [project]
      name = "mypackage"
      version = "1.0.0"
      description = "A well-structured Python package"
      readme = "README.md"
      requires-python = ">=3.8"
      license = "MIT"
      authors = [
          {name = "Your Name", email = "your.email@example.com"}
      ]
      dependencies = [
          "requests>=2.28.0",
          "pyyaml~=6.0",
      ]
      
      [project.optional-dependencies]
      test = [
          "pytest>=7.0.0",
          "pytest-cov>=4.0.0",
      ]
      dev = [
          "black>=23.0.0",
          "mypy>=1.0.0",
      ]
      
      [project.scripts]
      mycli = "mypackage.cli:main"
      
      # Directory structure
      mypackage/
      ├── src/
      │   └── mypackage/
      │       ├── __init__.py
      │       ├── core.py
      │       └── cli.py
      ├── tests/
      │   └── test_core.py
      ├── pyproject.toml
      ├── README.md
      └── LICENSE

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
  tags: ["python", "packaging", "distribution"]
</rule> 